  <div class="content-callout">
    <h2>The Short Answer</h2>
    <p>
      Pick <strong>ByteSIM</strong> if you need a real local phone number for calls and texts, not just data, in one of its supported countries. Pick <strong>UPeSIM</strong> if you just want cheap prepaid data with zero identity checks and a code that actually gives you the full discount it advertises. They're not really competing for the same trip: one sells a number, the other sells data you can install weeks ahead of time.
    </p>
  </div>

  <h2>The Core Difference: A Real Phone Number vs. Pure Prepaid Data</h2>
  <p>
    ByteSIM's whole pitch is bundling a real local number (calls, texts, hotspot, a local IP address) on top of data, in select countries including the US, Canada, UK, France, Spain, Australia, Vietnam, South Korea, and Thailand. Getting that number means identity verification: a passport photo and a selfie, standard for getting an actual phone number in most countries. UPeSIM doesn't offer a number at all. It's a French MVNO selling strictly data-only, prepaid, no subscription, and no ID check of any kind, in 200+ countries and territories.
  </p>
  <p>
    That makes this less of a head-to-head and more of a "what do you actually need" question. If you only want data and don't want to hand over a passport photo, UPeSIM is the simpler buy almost everywhere. If you specifically need a working local number to receive a verification text or make a local call, ByteSIM is the only one of the two that solves that at all, but only in its supported countries.
  </p>

  <h2>Spain, Side by Side</h2>
  <div class="content-box">
    <table>
      <thead>
        <tr>
          <th></th>
